---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Text from '@/components/Text/Text.astro';
import Anchor from '@/components/Anchor/Anchor.astro';
import { communityLinks } from '@/data/community';
---

<Layout
  title="About LibreCourseUY — Non-Profit FOSS Community in Uruguay"
  description="LibreCourseUY is a non-profit free and open source software community based in Uruguay. Learn how we are organized, who owns the projects, and how to take part."
>
  <main class="flex min-h-screen flex-col items-start justify-start gap-12 py-16">
    <section class="w-full space-y-4">
      <Text variant="h1">About LibreCourseUY</Text>
      <Text variant="p" class="max-w-3xl text-muted">
        LibreCourseUY is a non-profit community based in Uruguay that helps programmers — from
        complete beginners to seasoned maintainers — contribute to free and open source software. We
        do it through real projects: no tutorials in isolation, no imaginary codebases.
      </Text>
    </section>

    <section class="w-full space-y-4">
      <Text variant="h2">What we do</Text>
      <ul class="max-w-3xl list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 text-muted">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-emphasis">Curate real projects.</strong> We keep a catalogue of open source
          projects built by members and organisations in the ecosystem, with the language, licence and
          contribution status of each one.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-emphasis">Teach the hard parts.</strong> Our guides cover the parts of open
          source nobody explains: gpg-signed commits, the Developer Certificate of Origin, Conventional
          Commits and a pull request that a maintainer can actually review.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-emphasis">Connect people.</strong> Discord is where questions get answered
          and where you find someone to pair with on your first issue.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="w-full space-y-4">
      <Text variant="h2">Why we exist</Text>
      <Text variant="p" class="max-w-3xl text-muted">
        Most people who want to contribute to open source do not lack motivation; they lack a first
        task they can finish. Tutorials end before the interesting part — the review, the rebase,
        the maintainer asking for a change — and without that part there is no contribution and no
        confidence. We built LibreCourseUY around the opposite order: join a real project, take a
        small issue, ship it with help, then take something bigger.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="p" class="max-w-3xl text-muted">
        The catalogue exists so that first step is concrete. Every entry lists its language,
        licence, maintainers and whether it is open to contributions, so nobody has to guess whether
        a project is alive or whether its author wants help. Organisations keep their own
        governance; the community provides the map, the guides and the people who answer questions.
      </Text>
    </section>

    <section class="w-full space-y-4">
      <Text variant="h2">How we are organized</Text>
      <Text variant="p" class="max-w-3xl text-muted">
        LibreCourseUY is not a company and does not claim ownership of members' work. Project owners
        keep ownership and governance of their projects; collaboration that happens through the
        community applies to the open source parts only. Private and commercial work stays private
        and commercial, and any arrangement around it is agreed directly between the people involved
        — the community is not a party to it.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="p" class="max-w-3xl text-muted">
        Contributions follow the rules of each repository: every commit carries a
        <Anchor href="/dco/">DCO sign-off</Anchor> and a GPG signature, and messages follow Conventional
        Commits. There is no membership fee, no contract and no gatekeeping beyond that.
      </Text>
    </section>

    <section class="w-full space-y-4">
      <Text variant="h2">Where the code lives</Text>
      <Text variant="p" class="max-w-3xl text-muted">
        Source lives on GitHub under the
        <Anchor href="https://github.com/LibreCourseUY">LibreCourseUY organisation</Anchor>, and
        activity across the ecosystem is tracked on
        <Anchor href={communityLinks.activity}>Gitsion</Anchor>. The organisations that maintain
        projects in the ecosystem are listed on the
        <Anchor href="/orgs/">organisations page</Anchor>.
      </Text>
    </section>

    <section class="w-full space-y-4">
      <Text variant="h2">Take part</Text>
      <Text variant="p" class="max-w-3xl text-muted">
        Read the <Anchor href="/contribute/">first contribution guide</Anchor>, pick something from
        the <Anchor href="/projects/">project catalogue</Anchor> and ask in
        <Anchor href={communityLinks.discord}>Discord</Anchor> when you get stuck. If you are still learning,
        the <Anchor href="/learn/">learning guide</Anchor> explains how to grow through real projects
        instead of exercises.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="p" class="max-w-3xl text-muted">
        For press, partnerships or anything that is not a code question, reach us in
        <Anchor href={communityLinks.discord}>Discord</Anchor> or open an issue on
        <Anchor href="https://github.com/LibreCourseUY">GitHub</Anchor>.
      </Text>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
